<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  IsekaiTraits_ExcludeFromRandomRoll.xml   Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-30
  ============================================================================

  ISEKAI_GRANT_EXCLUSION_1, owner's ruling: our Star-Wars identity traits
  (IsekaiTraits_StarWarsReflavor.xml reflavors Isekai_Protagonist/Antagonist
  to "Chosen One"/"Dark Side Ascendant" — Force-fiction identity) must not be
  dispensed by blind chance. Identity arrives via backstories/play only:
  Hero's Awakening Scroll and Villain's Mask (both explicit CompUseEffect
  grants, unaffected by commonality) are the intended route.

  READ THE MECHANISM FIRST (standing lesson) — there are TWO independent
  random-roll pathways, not one:

  (1) VANILLA pawn generation reads the TraitDef's own <commonality> field
      directly for every pawn generated anywhere in the game (colonists,
      wanderers, prisoners, raiders). Source read 2026-08-30, workshop
      3657580708 Defs/TraitDefs/IsekaiTraits.xml: Isekai_Protagonist and
      Isekai_Antagonist both ship commonality=0.01 ("Extremely rare natural
      roll, also earned via [scroll/mask]" — a DELIBERATE upstream choice we
      are overriding). CLOSED by this patch: commonality -> 0, mirroring the
      convention every Isekai_Rank_* trait already uses ("Never randomly
      assigned" per RankTraits.xml) for exactly this "earned only" pattern.
      Explicit grants (CompUseEffect_IsekaiTrait.DoEffect -> AddIsekaiTrait ->
      Trait.GainTrait) call GainTrait directly and never consult commonality,
      so the scroll/mask still work identically after this patch.

  (2) ISEKAI's OWN NPC trait roller, IsekaiTraitHelper.RollRandomTraits
      (Source/IsekaiLeveling/Core/IsekaiTraitHelper.cs), is called from
      PawnStatGenerator.InitializePawnStats for every pawn the mod's own
      component initializes. It reads a HARDCODED C# dictionary
      (TraitCommonality, mirroring the same 0.01/0.01 values) — NOT the live
      TraitDef.commonality field. This patch (an XML edit) CANNOT reach that
      pathway; no PatchOperation touches C# state. Reflected in the item's
      progress note as a separate, smaller residual gap (needs a Harmony
      reflection patch removing Protagonist/Antagonist from the private
      static RollableTraits list — not attempted here, no existing Jawa_
      Harmony-patch DLL to host it in cheaply). Actual exposure through this
      path is small (0.01 weight among dozens of candidates, itself gated
      behind an 80%-chance-of-zero roll) but nonzero.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>ISEKAI RPG LEVELING</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/TraitDef[defName="Isekai_Protagonist"]/commonality</xpath>
          <value><commonality>0</commonality></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/TraitDef[defName="Isekai_Antagonist"]/commonality</xpath>
          <value><commonality>0</commonality></value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
